From 3a0de1467828642dc070d3063502527f87311895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xtu-glm53 <xtu@local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 17:19:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] feat(GLM5.3/SM80): bind SM8x sparse-MLA backend for
 glm5next DSA layers

GLM-5.3-Flash's 11 sparse-MLA (DSA) layers go through the generic
FlashMLASparseImpl stack, whose kernels require SM90+. On an sm8x card the
platform candidate pool is empty, so the model cannot build. Add a scoped
SM8x backend that reuses FlashMLASparse's bf16 gather / logical->physical
topk machinery and swaps only the final attention kernel for the portable
Triton sparse_mla_fwd_with_sink added in the previous commit.

- flashmla_sparse_sm8x.py (new): FlashMLASparseSM8XBackend/Impl. bf16 KV only,
  head sizes {512 (NoPE), 576}, capability major 8. The impl also concatenates
  (q_nope, q_pe) in torch, because the CUDA concat_mla_q kernel hard-requires
  rope_dim == 64 and GLM-5.3 is rope-free (qk_rope_head_dim == 0).
- layers/mla.py: MLAModules gains an optional attn_backend (default None) that
  is forwarded to MLAAttention, which already accepted it. Every existing
  caller leaves it None, so auto-selection is unchanged.
- glm5next/nvidia/attention.py: binds the backend when sm8x_sparse_mla_enabled()
  and the KV cache is not quantized (fp8/fp4 stays on the normal path so it
  fails closed with the standard 'no valid backend' error).

No compatibility impact on other models: MLAModules' new field defaults to
None; the only model that reads it is glm5next; the new backend is reachable
solely through that explicit binding.

Verified: imports OK for vllm / deepseek_v4 / deepseek_v41 / glm5next;
backend reports name FLASHMLA_SPARSE_SM8X, head sizes [512, 576], cap 8.x only,
and rejects a non-bf16 KV cache.

(cherry picked from commit b26780f5b1629cdf2b2b43fdf31ed1f93c388731)
